What this is

A small P2P demo system that implements an event-sourced peer network with cryptographic signing, a trust (DAG/RealBond) graph and a Byzantine-ready consensus layer — aimed at experimenting with meetings/commitments, reputation and gossip-based dissemination. It’s a demo / prototype used by developers to explore event creation, storage, trust scoring and gossip/consensus flows.
Stack

    Language(s): HTML (UI/docs/prototypes) + Go (core runtime)
    Framework / runtime: Go 1.21
    Notable libraries / dependencies: golang.org/x/crypto (ed25519 usage and crypto helpers). The design is shaped by the repo’s internal packages: pkg/terra (EventBus), pkg/data (EventStore / StateEngine), pkg/network (GossipNode / DAGManager), pkg/consensus (consensus layer), pkg/sec (key management).

