How it fits together:

    The runtime entry is cmd/node — main.go creates a KeyManager (pkg/sec), starts an EventBus (pkg/terra) to publish events, appends those events into an EventStore (pkg/data) and feeds a StateEngine (pkg/data) to compute state. For networking it uses pkg/network (GossipNode + DAGManager) to discover peers and build trust graphs; pkg/consensus runs proposals and voting over events. Events are defined in pkg/core (ID/hash/signature/payload model) and signed with ed25519. The HTML files in the repo are documentation and dashboard prototypes that illustrate system architecture and visualizations.

How to run it

Requirements: Go 1.21+, network port 6024 may be used by the gossip node.

Shortest path:

    Clone and fetch modules:
    Code

    git clone https://github.com/60-24/Html-P2P-60-24-.git
    cd Html-P2P-60-24-
    go mod download

    Build and run the node demo:
    Code

    go run ./cmd/node

    or
    Code

    go build -o p2p-node ./cmd/node
    ./p2p-node

Notes:

    The main demo (cmd/node/main.go) performs the Session #2 event system demo (key generation, publish events, append to EventStore, compute state). The code shows port 6024 used by GossipNode in session3 demo; running in constrained/test environments may fail to bind or discover peers.
    There are no obvious external secrets required (keys are generated at runtime by pkg/sec), but the network demo expects to bind a port and may attempt peer operations.
    Tests: there is at least one test file (pkg/core/event_test.go) — run go test ./... to execute package tests.

